{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1144113-a-deathlord-as-mentor-teacher-for-a-solar","id":1144113,"title":"A Deathlord as Mentor/Teacher for a Solar","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-26T10:20:52-07:00","id":1144113,"title":"A Deathlord as Mentor/Teacher for a Solar","content":"So, earlier today, I was reading Tanith Lee's Death's Master. It got me thinking about the Deathlords in a very different context than I had ever done: not as antagonists, but as possible allies or sources of power, even for a Solar that does not betray Creation.<br /> <br /> The Deathlords are, in essence, the most powerful dead things the player characters will encounter, unless they want to go talk to the Neverborn.<br /> However, they are also remnants of the First Age. They have knowledge of many powerful spells, artifacts and other things a young Solar would love to know.<br /> \u200b<br /> A comparison that I consider adequate is to the Third Circle Demons. They are equally dangerous (some more than others), both groups have access to stuff new Solars need to build a power base, and with the right persuasion, both are probably willing to offer such aid. <br /> <br /> There is, of course, a major difference: the Demon Princes have not all sworn to destroy Creation. While there are plenty of Demons who would love nothing more than to turn Creation into a hellscape, not all necessary enemies of the Solars (take Amalion, for example). <b>However, most young Solars will not know that the Deathlords are out to destroy the world. A clever Deathlord might trick the Solar to believe they have amiable goals.</b><br /> <br /> Now, such a teacher-student relationship would be campaign changing. And I fully expect that once the full scope of a Deathlord's ambitions is revealed, the Solar will rethink their allegiances. <br /> However, I think such a story could be very cool too, without immediately having to resort to the Deathlord forcing the Solar to become an Abyssal, or trying to murder them because they might one day become a powerful enemy.<br /> <br /> So, now that I've gotten all that out of my system: what do you think? Is there a place in Exalted for Deathlords beside antagonists? Or am I just crazy and is this a stupid idea?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8097-wern212","name":"wern212","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T11:07:44-07:00","id":1144130,"title":"","content":"Actually yeah. Heck this was actually pointed out in one of the 2nd edition books. Not in the same terms you did, but that individual Deathlords have probably forgotten more about some subjects than the collective setting has known for centuries. I mean it would probably not be too much of a stretch for even a new exalt to ask, &quot;Okay I appreciate the help, but what are you really getting out of this?&quot; The Deathlord in question is almost invariably using the PC for something, but that could just as easily be screwing over a rival, or entertaining itself, as it could be a case of &quot;You will show that piece of crap who's the greatest commander in the world.&quot; <br /> &quot;Me?&quot;<br /> &quot;Sure, but actually me as I will be teaching you everything you know.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T11:15:59-07:00","id":1144132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Deathlords are, in essence, the most powerful dead things the player characters will encounter, unless they want to go talk to the Neverborn. </div> </div> </div>Technically, Solar exalted have a decent chance to meet several celestial gods too and perhaps even Gaia, so... =P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T11:42:48-07:00","id":1144143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wern212</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1144113-a-deathlord-as-mentor-teacher-for-a-solar#post1144113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> However, most young Solars will not know that the Deathlords are out to destroy the world\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming, of course, that said Deathlords <i>are</i> &quot;out to destroy the world.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T11:46:49-07:00","id":1144148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1144113-a-deathlord-as-mentor-teacher-for-a-solar?p=1144132#post1144132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Technically, Solar exalted have a decent chance to meet several celestial gods too and perhaps even Gaia, so... =P</div> </div> </div> </div>Are they dead?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T12:23:55-07:00","id":1144162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1144113-a-deathlord-as-mentor-teacher-for-a-solar?p=1144143#post1144143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming, of course, that said Deathlords <i>are</i> &quot;out to destroy the world.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>A good point. Though I doubt a lot of Deathlords have truly pleasant goals for Creation.<br /> But you are correct, not all Deathlords consider destroying Creation their purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8097-wern212","name":"wern212","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T12:38:30-07:00","id":1144172,"title":"","content":"In some ways most of the deathlords seem to be more like a kid who gets told to go clean his room and ends up playing with all his action figures for hours while telling his mom he's working really hard on the whole 'clean the room' idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T13:04:23-07:00","id":1144177,"title":"","content":"To my mind, the First Age experience that would make Deathlords so attractive as mentors would also be a firm basis for making them willing.<br /> <br /> \u200bNot about some kind of scheme, but because the character(s) evoke strong memories of earlier times, and just this once, on a whim, they decide to indulge in nostalgia.<br /> <br /> \u200bMind, if it was my story, I would plan on this being part of an arc in which the indulgence ultimately just leads back around into their loathing of life in general and their own lives in particular; they help and teach you briefly because of a relatively short stirring of memory, but ultimately it just leads them back to recalling everything they hate, and projecting it on you specifically.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt depends on the story if that ultimately turns them into a personal enemy, or they remain in the role of a mentor, just one who has become cold, distant and venomous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T13:05:19-07:00","id":1144178,"title":"","content":"A sneaky Deathlord pretending to be some fallen god from the underworld (to explain the necrotic essence) - guiding a circle of players to do certain things in a xanatos gambit to mess with his opponent deathlords and strengthen his power base?<br /> <br /> sure<br /> <br /> &quot;Hey, see that deathlord over there? he's bad news! Go kick his butt! I'll be over here taking over his operations as you kick him out of them&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T19:30:37-07:00","id":1144258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1144113-a-deathlord-as-mentor-teacher-for-a-solar?p=1144177#post1144177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To my mind, the First Age experience that would make Deathlords so attractive as mentors would also be a firm basis for making them willing.<br /> <br /> \u200bNot about some kind of scheme, but because the character(s) evoke strong memories of earlier times, and just this once, on a whim, they decide to indulge in nostalgia.<br /> <br /> \u200bMind, if it was my story, I would plan on this being part of an arc in which the indulgence ultimately just leads back around into their loathing of life in general and their own lives in particular; they help and teach you briefly because of a relatively short stirring of memory, but ultimately it just leads them back to recalling everything they hate, and projecting it on you specifically.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt depends on the story if that ultimately turns them into a personal enemy, or they remain in the role of a mentor, just one who has become cold, distant and venomous.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love this idea. And I hope my GM isn't reading this post. :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11847-kfinigan","name":"KFinigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T23:34:56-07:00","id":1144300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KFinigan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1144113-a-deathlord-as-mentor-teacher-for-a-solar?p=1144258#post1144258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I love this idea. And I hope my GM isn't reading this post. :-)</div> </div> </div> </div>To the contrary, if you wanted to implement this, wouldn't it be all the better if your GM saw this and was sold on the idea by the time you brought it up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12682-remedy","name":"Remedy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T00:12:12-07:00","id":1144303,"title":"","content":"Isn't the premise of the OP basically the canon situation with that Solar Admiral from Skullstone? <br /> The Deathlords acting as mentors would probably be no worse in the long run than some powerful but ambiguous diety like Amoth Citysmiter. While they are nominally supposed to destroy Creation they have so consistently drug their feet on the whole project and their current plans are so oblique to that goal that it can probably be dismissed as a pressing issue for all but the longest running campaigns.<br /> <br /> As for the specifics, it is important to remember that all of the Deathlords were raised with a First Age worldview. While they are no longer Solars, the notion that an alliance of semi-independent Exalted monarchies where the individual Chosen use their dominions as a means to pursue their individual goals and aggrandizement probably makes a great deal of sense to them. Its effectively how they behave now. The Second Age might strike them as wrong or disturbing on a visceral level that is hard for most people to understand.<br /> <br /> The melodrama of death might mean that the Deathlords cannot bring themselves to &quot;take the win&quot; while Creation is in the state it is in and that they seek to elevate Exalted, especially Abyssals and Solars, back into their &quot;proper&quot; place so that when the Deathlords do finally move into the end game of their goals the situation is the appropriate epic struggle they need it to be.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T02:17:21-07:00","id":1144316,"title":"","content":"Moray Darktide is a Solar with a Deathlord boss (well, god/prophet), but it's not quite the same as the situation wern212 is describing.<br /> <br /> Or rather, the Silver Prince is tricking everyone into thinking he's a... well, a Bodhisattva. He's made his own religion (which is not all trickery, to be fair, and probably isn't dramatically different from the traditional beliefs of people living in a huge shadowland), of which he's the leader, and Moray Darktide is essentially a culture hero, of a culture that worships the Bodhisattva.<br /> The Silver Prince isn't tricking Moray specifically into thinking he's just trying to lead Skullstone into a glorious future which definitely doesn't involve total oblivion*, he's tricking <i>everyone</i> into thinking that.<br /> <br /> <br /> *I imagine the 3rd ed version of this is going to be quite different. Though the religion of Skullstone may be quite similar: perhaps the Bodhisattva's goal is to simply be worshipped, and spread Skullstone's empire and faithful to gain more and more converts. Or maybe he genuinely just wants to spread a Shadowland so the living and dead are united. We'll see.<br /> It hardly needs saying that Island 5 won't be making a reappearance.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T03:05:37-07:00","id":1144325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1144113-a-deathlord-as-mentor-teacher-for-a-solar?p=1144148#post1144148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are they dead?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why, there are no more portals to Yu-shan in 3rd edition? =p<br /> Of course, meeting Gaia could be hard but it's plenty of other elder gods well disposed toward Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13673,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","user":"Maris Streck","date":". 09-27-2017, 06:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T03:15:47-07:00","id":1144327,"title":"","content":"Wern212 said &quot;the most powerful <b>dead</b> thing the PCs will encounter.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T03:49:04-07:00","id":1144336,"title":"","content":"Deathlords might have some grudges that align with solar ones like in 2nd ed. Mask of the winters have/may have with heaven /sidereals.. he may take under his wing poor young solar hunted by wyld hunt/sidereals. Then explain him his situation and offer help training and safe base/home.<br /> Similiar thing might been tryed by unquestionables in malfeas after usurpation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4588-ludek","name":"Ludek","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T05:29:26-07:00","id":1144353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1144113-a-deathlord-as-mentor-teacher-for-a-solar?p=1144316#post1144316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> *I imagine the 3rd ed version of this is going to be quite different. Though the religion of Skullstone may be quite similar: perhaps the Bodhisattva's goal is to simply be worshipped, and spread Skullstone's empire and faithful to gain more and more converts. Or maybe he genuinely just wants to spread a Shadowland so the living and dead are united. We'll see.<br /> It hardly needs saying that Island 5 won't be making a reappearance.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI think there can be an interesting middle ground; where it's not as straightforward as the Bodhisattva's religion just being a ruse to harvest the soulsteel he needs to build his giant death fleet, but it's about something more than just expanding a territory. Examination of what the implications of a religion rooted so deeply in exaltation of death, both in terms of what it means for adherents, and what social forces could be going on behind willingness to convert at large.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat might also speak to something a Solar could be mentored in; philosophies of fatalism and the macabre. You're still distinct from an Abyssal if you don't fully embody it, but there might be room for a Solar to believe some of it, or at least be listening. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T05:29:48-07:00","id":1144354,"title":"","content":"I'm really quite fond of the idea of a Deathlord being a mentor for a Solar. If Deathlords are still the megaswole ultraghosts of First-Age Solars, a Deathlord could perhaps be mentoring a Solar who holds the Exaltation the Deathlord once held, or that of someone important to the Deathlord's prior life. Not that it's a requirement, but it's full of potential.<br /> <br /> I also am fond of the idea of Deathlords trading their tutelage and knowledge of ancient stuff for service and information about modern stuff. It's like when Grandpa needs your help with his computer, but instead of giving you a fistful of Werther's Originals, he teaches you how to RULE THE WORRRRRRLD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T08:01:15-07:00","id":1144772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1144113-a-deathlord-as-mentor-teacher-for-a-solar?p=1144327#post1144327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wern212 said &quot;the most powerful <b>dead</b> thing the PCs will encounter.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>oh, my bad, derped out a word .-.<br /> Anyhow sure, there's a lot of reasons for a Dreadlord to teach a Solar. Of course, manipulation, gaining trust, etc are all excellent reasons for they to spend time with a Solar, just like promising forbidden knowledge is an excellent way to gain some special service from the ones that should be their most bitter enemies. But even better is IMHO offering tainted knowledge, such as charms or spells specifically designed to help the dreadlord (i.e. some power that creates ghosts when it slays an enemy, especially if the ghost is secretly bound to the Dreadlord).<br /> <br /> In the end just remember that Dreadlords are formidable planners, with 7+ mental and social stats. Their plans are flawless, their lies supernaturally persuasive and they're really, really good at making you do whatever they need to bring their plans forward and having you pay for them as if it were a fair trade.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T08:28:25-07:00","id":1144784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1144113-a-deathlord-as-mentor-teacher-for-a-solar?p=1144772#post1144772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But even better is IMHO offering tainted knowledge, such as charms or spells specifically designed to help the dreadlord (i.e. some power that creates ghosts when it slays an enemy, especially if the ghost is secretly bound to the Dreadlord).</div> </div> </div> </div>That isn't really how powers such as that work in this system or setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the end just remember that Dreadlords are formidable planners, with 7+ mental and social stats. Their plans are flawless, their lies supernaturally persuasive and they're really, really good at making you do whatever they need to bring their plans forward and having you pay for them as if it were a fair trade.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI think there are issues to approaching any character in this way. For one thing, it would require a Storyteller to actually come up with flawless plans (an infamously dicey proposition when dealing with players, and particularly in a game such as Exalted), or else arbitrate their own success via fiat.<br /> <br /> \u200bI also say it would be the kind of thing that puts a lot of players off interacting with the premise in the first place, to have a combination of &quot;Deathlords will want to screw you over, and will almost definitely succeed&quot;. Where can you really go with that?<br /> <br /> \u200bBesides, it doesn't really gel with how the Deathlords have ever been even intentionally portrayed, with a consistent theme of being perverse and maniacal in a manner that results in a lot of plans that are severely flawed, often to the point of being virtually self-defeating. One of the iconic actions of a Deathlord in the setting, the Mask of Winters conquering Thorns, is often referred to as a bit of a dumb move that his fellows are angry at him for because it's given a lot of their game away to the world.<br /> <br /> \u200bSome of the specifics of that might be changed a bit (Lord knows they actually need a bit of credibility returned to them), but I doubt the writers will want to go for the Deathlords being so thoroughly in control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T10:40:38-07:00","id":1144830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1144113-a-deathlord-as-mentor-teacher-for-a-solar?p=1144784#post1144784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That isn't really how powers such as that work in this system or setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends. Deathlords have all the knowledge and had all the required time to develop unique powers and spells. Just like the Broken Winged Crane offers flawed rituals and a very high chance to turn the reader into a Yozi servant so a Deathlord has everything he needs for whatever he wants to do. He's not all-powerful and still has some ironclad limitations, but cmon, you know what I mean.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bI think there are issues to approaching any character in this way. For one thing, it would require a Storyteller to actually come up with flawless plans (an infamously dicey proposition when dealing with players, and particularly in a game such as Exalted), or else arbitrate their own success via fiat. </div> </div> </div>Just saying: you're working for your own interest with a very elaborate plan fueled by virtually endless resources. Of course that the players are supposed to thwart the villain's plan somehow, but a deathlord is the kind of villain that outmaneuvers you in a lot of battles before you have the chance to hurt him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bBesides, it doesn't really gel with how the Deathlords have ever been even intentionally portrayed, with a consistent theme of being perverse and maniacal in a manner that results in a lot of plans that are severely flawed, often to the point of being virtually self-defeating. One of the iconic actions of a Deathlord in the setting, the Mask of Winters conquering Thorns, is often referred to as a bit of a dumb move that his fellows are angry at him for because it's given a lot of their game away to the world.. </div> </div> </div>This is a bit controversial... Mask of Winter gave away how dangerous the deathlords are, but in doing so he still obtained a strong foothold in Creation, outclassing almost all his other peers. Other deathlords are mostly envious because he reaped the benefits of striking first. After all, reaching oblivion in 500 or in 5000 years has little significance for immortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T11:01:27-07:00","id":1146102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Remedy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1144113-a-deathlord-as-mentor-teacher-for-a-solar?p=1144300#post1144300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To the contrary, if you wanted to implement this, wouldn't it be all the better if your GM saw this and was sold on the idea by the time you brought it up?</div> </div> </div> </div>I love the idea. I'm not sure I want it used in our game for my character or another...... we have enough complications that we've made for ourselves. ;-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11847-kfinigan","name":"KFinigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T19:20:38-07:00","id":1146524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wern212</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1144113-a-deathlord-as-mentor-teacher-for-a-solar#post1144113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>However, most young Solars will not know that the Deathlords are out to destroy the world. A clever Deathlord might trick the Solar to believe they have amiable goals.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI was thinking some more about the Deathlords in general, and came back to this question. It occurred to me that in certain instances, the distinction between these two points might not be clear, some of the standards might not be the focus of the Deathlord, and trickery might not be necessary.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm thinking something different even from &quot;the Deathlord believes that destroying the world is a good thing&quot;; more like the Deathlord is doing something that they believe to be good (after a manner of speaking) that also has a capacity to end all life that they are indifferent to. The idea of a Deathlord openly and honestly presenting you with something significant and apparently beneficial, where it would take your own foresight and introspection to say &quot;wait, is this really good for me/the world&quot;.<br /> <br /> \u200bI was wondering about the Lover Clad in the Raiment of Tears; the idea that she draws on people who have an emptiness within them, or are engaged in patterns of behaviour that are momentarily pleasurable but ultimately numbing, and feeds into them. Not necessarily with an underhanded, malicious goal with the specific intention of destroying everybody, but more like the ultimate self-destruction not really being focused on.<br /> <br /> \u200bWith the Lover specifically, I have a notion in which she presents many guises to be a figure whom the lost, the forelorn and the hollow can pour their love and devotion into, and who can in turn provide them with reliefs and purposes that will ultimately just lead them to ruin. To some she's a provider of stimulations that ultimately just reinforce one's emptiness until it consumes them, but I'd say there's also room in there for a glorious warrior queen to whom people can pledge themselves and seek glorious conquest and personal deaths to lay at her feet, as well as something like a religious figure who embraces the lost and provides them with hollow comforts that ultimately just reinforce the state that they're currently in, and lead them to wallow in that rather than pursue self-improvement or self-love.<br /> <br /> \u200bA Deathlord such as that might be a really sincere, open and powerful mentor, it's just that what she's teaching you is either reinforcing some of the worst things about yourself, or is guiding you along your own possible path to bringing ruin to everything around you.<br /> <br /> Hmm, I don't think I'm making my point very well, and rambling about a bit.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm just trying to figure out an application arising from the statement that you can be sincerely loved by (and yourself love) somebody whose actions towards you are nevertheless slowly killing you. A sense of nuances in which there's a Deathlord who is not being dishonest with you, and whose compelling philosophy is a few steps to the side of &quot;top 13 reasons why all life should be brought to an end&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T19:32:35-07:00","id":1146530,"title":"","content":"A point to bring up as well Solars aren't exactly guaranteed to have noble goals or the like. I mean 2nd edition there was a Solar who's big goal involved feeding the world to a carrion eating god, so some Solars might end up more amicable to the Deathlord mentioning their big goal as ordained by their bosses is killing the world. Or a Solar might not be against destroying a certain person, place, or organization. Could totally see a Solar signing on for training and assistance from the most of the Deathlords (probably regretting it immensely with some of them down the line.) once it's clear the Deathlord is on board with the plan.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T21:38:33-07:00","id":1146566,"title":"","content":"The nature of the disagreement between the Solar and the Deathlord might be openly discussed and accepted by both of them. <br /> A mentee of the Bishop might have a philosophy which is remarkably similar to Buddhism without the nihilistic bent the DL usually espouses. The two could agree on the matter of attachment leading to suffering but draw subtly but importantly different conclusions and discuss the matter amicably.<br /> <br /> This being Exalted there may be a kung fu duel over it at some point, but that is almost incidental.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}